## Governing issue

Refs #7

PR #22 merged into `master` as merge commit `20b1119aee23d4441dfcee279a2408c1ee3b2e3e`. This PR targets exact base `master@20b1119aee23d4441dfcee279a2408c1ee3b2e3e`. The original four issue #7 commits and published CRLF correction `5ccec8c1a694a6640bc098c2ee1e1a065cb9cd9f` were not rewritten. Automated review on `5ccec8c1` found three validator defects, the ready-triggered review on `e2009083` found two additional private-path coverage gaps, the subsequent exact-head review on `2ca0b87` found the root-home variant, the full review on `0771f7b` found three runner and fixture-contract gaps, and the full review on `faed501` found two exact-suite and inventory gaps; twelve single-concern correction commits were appended.

Current head is `01cbfcc1052ade4d2dccfb26299cb61a3672f804`, the PR contains sixteen issue #7 commits, the merge base remains `9080bd15d0cd09999dda5987a9d90d3c6b9f75b3`, and the diff contains 15 issue #7 files.

## Scope

Establish the downstream SDK regression boundary in sixteen independently green commits:

1. `30667d9` — compose the accepted logger-path and FastCRC tests under one standalone CMake/CTest root;
2. `f8c1501` — add the checked ownership, CRC-profile, FastCRC-usage, and hermetic-fixture manifest with fail-closed negative controls;
3. `b17d6c8` — add the one-command Release/strict-sanitizer runner and require the deliberate sanitizer control;
4. `aa62bea` — require exact regression ownership in reviewer-readable pull-request intake;
5. `5ccec8c` — canonicalize CRLF only at the checked text-hash boundary while retaining a fail-closed content-change control;
6. `6af41e2` — restrict fixture policy checks to Git-tracked repository inputs so in-tree build outputs remain valid;
7. `9a95c04` — detect ordinary single-backslash and forward-slash Windows user paths;
8. `e200908` — inventory FastCRC calls made through pointer member access;
9. `9be28ee` — recognize developer-specific macOS `/Users/<name>/` paths;
10. `2ca0b87` — scan every Git-tracked test input for private absolute paths;
11. `0771f7b` — recognize developer-specific `/root/` paths without making the validator match its own policy source;
12. `7223f78` — align the common runner contract with its actual CMake/CTest 3.20 interface floor;
13. `6f7ff4a` — require custom CMake and CTest executables as an explicit pair and register runner controls;
14. `faed501` — replace the incomplete artifact denylist with a finite UTF-8 source/text allowlist and Git-mode controls;
15. `fe9ef8b` — require exact normal and sanitizer CTest discovery sets before execution;
16. `01cbfcc` — inventory source-relative paths ending in the authoritative FastCRC header.

No production SDK source or existing accepted behavior assertion changes in this PR. The twelve corrective commits change only downstream test infrastructure, its build entrypoint, controls, manifest, and documentation.

The CMake/docs and CMake/SDK-test path combinations are inseparable within their owning commits: the documented entrypoint is the contract for the exact test graph, and the checked registry must consume the exact CTest names created by that graph. Each mixed commit contains the required `Combined concerns` section.

## Provenance

The suite composition, manifest, validator, runner, fixture conventions, review guard, and supporting tests are downstream project-owned MIT-licensed work authored by OpenAI Codex.

This PR only adopts existing tests through the common interface:

- the logger-path regression retains its existing project notice and accepted behavior;
- the FastCRC regression and negative control retain the provenance recorded by #6 / PR #22;
- the FastCRC source adaptation remains derived from MicroStar-Tech/Livox-SDK2 commit `22d7d10e2918bfaa3e0b9a07532f19b41da1adbe`, authored by Xuqing Liu under the retained Frank Bösing MIT notice.

No external branch, moving repository, raw capture, firmware file, private device/network data, or license-unknown corpus is imported.

## Compatibility

No public API, ABI, wire layout, packet behavior, production build target, packaging, dependency, or consumer runtime behavior changes.

The manifest locks the accepted profiles independently:

- `fastcrc_livox_compatibility`: CCITT-FALSE `0x29B1`, Livox seed-`0` mcrf4xx `0x2189`, CRC-32/ISO-HDLC `0xCBF43926`;
- `fastcrc_standard_reference`: seed-`0xFFFF` MCRF4XX `0x6F91`, explicitly not firmware-file authority.

Normal execution is Release without sanitizers. The common runner requires CMake and CTest 3.20 or newer; custom executables must be supplied as an explicit `--cmake` and `--ctest` pair. The normal graph contains five tests and the strict graph contains six. Strict sanitizer mode is supported on GCC- and Clang-compatible compilers; unavailable native platform cells remain pending rather than inferred. Tracked files below `tests` must be regular UTF-8 source/text files in the checked allowlist; binary fixtures require a reviewed policy change.

## Regression ownership

This infrastructure PR adds the checked source-contract inventory and does not change production SDK behavior.

- `logger_path_portability` → exact CTest `livox_logger_path_tests`, with native Windows and Unix trigger;
- `fastcrc_livox_compatibility` → exact CTest `livox_fastcrc_tests`, with supported compiler/data-model trigger;
- `macos_native_discovery_bind` → platform-only owner `pOmelchenko`, repeated for macOS networking changes and consumer qualification;
- `firmware_header_checksum_fixture` → pending owner `pOmelchenko`, triggered by #11 checksum parameters and an approved redistributable fixture;
- `fastcrc_portable_bulk_loads` → pending owner `pOmelchenko`, triggered when #12 lands its focused portability, used-span, and performance regression.

The checked FastCRC subsection accounts for four include consumers and eight core/sample call sites with method, exact or bounded span, object lifetime, and owning regression. Header-surface changes, new consumers/calls, and public exposure fail the manifest check until explicitly reviewed.

