## Summary

Add a versioned claim-bearing admission layer around the merged experimental domain covariance calibration v1 without changing any v1 content identities.

- use a conservative default transform grid with covariance scale >= 1;
- reject custom shrinkage grids unless the frozen policy explicitly allows them;
- bind covariance dimension, coordinate frame, physical unit, query type, and horizon semantics;
- add independent finite-group gates for practical mean leave-one-group-out Gaussian-NLL improvement, held-group win fraction, worst-group harm, and group count;
- require a matching content-addressed `EvidenceDecisionV1` rather than a naked application Boolean;
- require the decision to be passing, confirmatory, claim/protocol matched, and above the frozen evidence-level threshold;
- optionally require `claim_authorized=true` for deployment policies;
- return the exact caller-owned covariance object on every rejected path; and
- bind the v2 certificate, semantics, evidence decision, v1 application, and actual input/output array digests in the application record.

## Compatibility

The existing `domain_covariance_calibration` module, schema version, defaults, APIs, and artifact identities are unchanged. The new module is experimental and is not exported from the frozen package root.

## Scientific boundary

This PR adds prospective infrastructure only. It does not establish calibrated uncertainty, improve a predictive mean, reopen the completed full-22 tournament, establish fresh-object transfer, support a Causal4D claim, authorize deployment, or establish state of the art. A separately registered independent calibration/evaluation study remains required.

## What changed

- defines a normalized two-band Möbius Vesica Piscis embedding with opposite chirality, one-turn breadth reversal, two-turn local return, and exact centerline contacts;
- proves exactly two centerline contacts at `(0, ±sqrt(3)/2, 0)`;
- reduces physical equality of the two single continuous boundary curves to the cubic `4*w*x^3 + 4*x^2 - 2*w*x - 3 = 0` on the viable height branch;
- uses exact rational Sturm arithmetic to prove two roots in `(-1,1)`, each with two boundary-turn preimages, for exactly four physical boundary contacts at the default quarter-turn phase;
- proves the alternate height branch contributes no contacts;
- independently recertifies the four-contact result at eight rational widths in `0 < w < 1/2`;
- emits twelve rigid local Seed-of-Life structural-pair placements without claiming a simultaneous seven-band realization;
- records an exact zero-contact obstruction for the current PR #174 half-turn phase inside this same standard-circular family, so the quarter-turn certificate is not silently transferred.

## Source boundary

The uploaded source note supplies the research target: one turn reverses side/orientation, two turns restore it, the centerlines meet twice, and the single continuous boundaries are claimed to meet four times. This PR treats those statements as testable geometry rather than established physics.

## Stack relationship

This is intentionally stacked on PR #174 (`agent/mobius-seed-of-life-v1`, head `eae0776de6436b495c8d8b27d139602fde963e43`). It targets that branch rather than `main` so the dependency and the phase-law conflict remain explicit.

